an the global $DEPLOYED baseline' — but only mcp/bot components are named","autodeploy.sh:504 `if changed \"$CONFIG_PATHS\"` diffs $DEPLOYED..$TARGET","autodeploy.sh:728/:751 obs/certbot blocks likewise diff via changed() from $DEPLOYED","On an incomplete tick the footer (763) that advances $SHA_FILE is skipped, so $DEPLOYED stays behind across the episode"],"finding":"The plan re-points only the review-bot delta gate to its per-component marker, but the config detect-only block and the host observability/certbot re-materialize blocks still compute `changed()` against the global $DEPLOYED. Because the global marker is not advanced on an incomplete tick, these blocks re-fire on every tick of an incomplete episode (re-emitting the config_manual marker / re-running the idempotent install scripts). The plan does not state whether re-firing them across an incomplete episode is intended and harmless.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7dd817714c633798","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Shape of the fix' (first bullet) vs autodeploy.sh:504,728,751","norm_id":"nc8c6f08b1e77fb7f","priority":0.275,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["mcp is in a backoff window (mcp_incomplete set) while a config path also changed in the same delta: every tick until the episode completes re-emits config_manual and re-runs install-observability/certbot"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a sentence noting these blocks remain gated on $DEPLOYED and re-fire idempotently across an incomplete episode by design (install scripts are idempotent; config_manual is a detect-only signal), so no correctness regression.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessaril